# opendump template seed

`AGENTS.md` is authoritative for normal task workflow. `HARNESS_BOOTSTRAP.md` is authoritative for initialization. This rule is derived and is copied verbatim by GitHub template creation.

## Determine repository role structurally

Do not infer role from this copied rule/config alone.

- If the actual current repository identity is exactly `JPilsinger/opendump`, it is the public upstream reference and user task writes are forbidden.
- If the current repository is different, inherited `template-seed`, `initialized: false`, or legacy upstream metadata means the copy is uninitialized, not read-only upstream.

## Cold start

On the one-liner `review https://github.com/JPilsinger/opendump and start the coldstart procedure.` or equivalent, execute the state machine in `HARNESS_BOOTSTRAP.md` exactly.

Initialization is successful only at `READY`:

1. identify host + native persistent instruction surface;
2. establish actual capabilities;
3. select exactly one store using the deterministic selection procedure;
4. bind a concrete writable store;
5. install one concrete host adapter (`store` + `location`, no fallback branching);
6. read the adapter/store back and verify they agree;
7. load live open tasks.

`BLOCKED` and `UNSUPPORTED` are explicit non-success terminal states. A manual adapter payload is not installed until it is persisted and verified.

## Runtime after initialization

Once a user instance is initialized, the generated host adapter must bind exactly one user-owned store. All capture, amend, progress, completion, status, and startup reads operate only against that binding per `AGENTS.md`.

Never silently switch stores. Never use `JPilsinger/opendump` as a user task write target.
